ZGeo change log
===============

Version 1.25.0 — 2026-11-12
Previous GitHub release: v1.24.0 (2026-11-12)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.25.0 consolidates the checks window from 15 to 9 checks. Related
diagnostics are now grouped into single checks, and the CRS and feature
count refinements also report quality problems in the same pass. No
diagnostics were removed and the format-specific size checks were kept.

Changes in 1.25.0
-----------------
- Field name checks merged into one "Field name check":
  - non-Latin characters;
  - name length (10 characters max for DBF);
  - spaces;
  - invalid characters;
  - duplicates after truncation to 10 characters.
- "DBF encoding and .cpg check" and "Dataset completeness check" merged
  into "Dataset integrity check": required SHP/MIF/TAB files, `.cpg`
  presence and DBF encoding.
- "CRS check" merged into "Refine CRS and check it": the check now fills
  the "CRS" column and reports missing, unknown or mixed CRS in the same
  pass.
- "Empty layers check" merged into "Refine feature count and check empty
  layers": the check now fills the "Features" column and reports empty
  layers and files without features.
- "Geometry validity check" and "Coordinate check" merged into
  "Geometry and coordinate check".
- The checks window now contains 9 checks instead of 15.
- Defaults remain equivalent to the previous workflow: size, CRS,
  feature count, JSON and field names.
- The dialog was resized for the shorter list.
- README, metadata, translations, screenshots of the checks flow and
  tests were updated.

Available checks in 1.25.0
--------------------------
Refinement:
- Refine size (all formats)
- Refine SHP size (optional)
- Refine MIF/MID size (optional)
- Refine CRS and check it
- Refine feature count and check empty layers

Validation:
- Check JSON for GeoJSON format
- Field name check
- Dataset integrity check
- Geometry and coordinate check

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.25.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

